{
  "title": "19: Maryam مريم",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nكٓهٰيٰعٓصٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\n\nKaf, Ha, Ya, ‘Ayn, Suad.\nذِكْرُ رَحْمَتِ رَبِّكَ عَبْدَهٗ زَكَرِيَّا ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(2)\n\n[This is] an account of your Lord’s mercy on His servant, Zechariah,\nاِذْ نَادٰى رَبَّهٗ نِدَآءً خَفِيًّا‏(3)\n\nwhen he called out to his Lord with a secret cry.\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّىْ وَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّاْسُ شَيْبًا وَّلَمْ اَكُنْۢ بِدُعَآئِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيًّا‏(4)\n\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Indeed my bones have become feeble, and my head has turned white with age, yet never have I, my Lord, been disappointed in supplicating You!\nوَاِنِّىْ خِفْتُ الْمَوَالِىَ مِنْ وَّرَآءِىْ وَكَانَتِ امْرَاَتِىْ عَاقِرًا فَهَبْ لِىْ مِنْ لَّدُنْكَ وَلِيًّا ۙ‏(5)\n\nIndeed I fear my kinsmen, after me, and my wife is barren. So grant me from Yourself an heir\nيَّرِثُنِىْ وَيَرِثُ مِنْ اٰلِ يَعْقُوْبَ ۖ  وَاجْعَلْهُ رَبِّ رَضِيًّا‏(6)\n\nwho may inherit from me and inherit from the House of Jacob, and make him, my Lord, pleasing [to You]!’\nيٰزَكَرِيَّاۤ اِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ بِغُلٰم اۨسْمُهٗ يَحْيٰى ۙ لَمْ نَجْعَلْ لَّهٗ مِنْ قَبْلُ سَمِيًّا‏(7)\n\n‘O Zechariah! Indeed We give you the good news of a son, whose name is ‘‘John.’’ Never before have We made anyone his namesake.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لِىْ غُلٰمٌ وَّكَانَتِ امْرَاَتِىْ عَاقِرًا وَّقَدْ بَلَغْتُ مِنَ الْكِبَرِ عِتِيًّا‏(8)\n\nHe said, ‘My Lord! How shall I have a son, when my wife is barren, and I am already advanced in age?’\nقَالَ كَذٰلِكَ‌ۚ قَالَ رَبُّكَ هُوَ عَلَىَّ هَيِّنٌ وَّقَدْ خَلَقْتُكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلَمْ تَكُ شَيْئًا‏(9)\n\nHe said, ‘So shall it be. Your Lord has said, ‘‘It is simple for Me.’’ Certainly I created you before when you were nothing.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اجْعَلْ لِّىْۤ اٰيَةً‌  ؕ قَالَ اٰيَتُكَ اَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ النَّاسَ ثَلٰثَ لَيَالٍ سَوِيًّا‏(10)\n\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Appoint a sign for me.’ He said, ‘Your sign is that you will not speak to the people for three complete nights.’\nفَخَرَجَ عَلٰى قَوْمِهٖ مِنَ الْمِحْرَابِ فَاَوْحٰٓى اِلَيْهِمْ اَنْ سَبِّحُوْا بُكْرَةً وَّعَشِيًّا‏(11)\n\nSo he emerged before his people from the Temple, and signalled to them that they should glorify [Allah] morning and evening.\nيٰيَحْيٰى خُذِ الْكِتٰبَ بِقُوَّةٍ‌ ؕ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ الْحُكْمَ صَبِيًّا ۙ‏(12)\n\n‘O John!’ [We said,] ‘Hold on with power to the Book!’ And We gave him judgement while still a child,\nوَّحَنَانًا مِّنْ لَّدُنَّا وَزَكٰوةً  ‌ؕ وَّكَانَ تَقِيًّا ۙ‏(13)\n\nand a compassion and purity from Us. He was Godwary\nوَّبَرًّۢا بِوَالِدَيْهِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ جَبَّارًا عَصِيًّا‏(14)\n\nand good to his parents, and was not self-willed or disobedient.\nوَسَلٰمٌ عَلَيْهِ يَوْمَ وُلِدَ وَيَوْمَ يَمُوْتُ وَيَوْمَ يُبْعَثُ حَيًّا‏(15)\n\nPeace be to him, the day he was born, and the day he dies, and the day he is raised alive!\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مَرْيَمَ‌ۘ اِذِ انْتَبَذَتْ مِنْ اَهْلِهَا مَكَانًا شَرْقِيًّا ۙ‏(16)\n\nAnd mention in the Book Mary, when she withdrew from her family to an easterly place.\nفَاتَّخَذَتْ مِنْ دُوْنِهِمْ حِجَابًا فَاَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهَا رُوْحَنَا فَتَمَثَّلَ لَهَا بَشَرًا سَوِيًّا‏(17)\n\nThus did she seclude herself from them, whereupon We sent to her Our Spirit and he became incarnate for her as a well-proportioned human.\nقَالَتْ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِالرَّحْمٰنِ مِنْكَ اِنْ كُنْتَ تَقِيًّا‏(18)\n\nShe said, ‘I seek the protection of the All-beneficent from you, should you be Godwary!’\n‌قَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا رَسُوْلُ رَبِّكِ ‌ ۖ  لِاَهَبَ لَكِ غُلٰمًا زَكِيًّا‏(19)\n\nHe said, ‘I am only a messenger of your Lord that I may give you a pure son.’\nقَالَتْ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لِىْ غُلٰمٌ وَّلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِىْ بَشَرٌ وَّلَمْ اَكُ بَغِيًّا‏(20)\n\nShe said, ‘How shall I have a child seeing that no human being has ever touched me, nor have I been unchaste?’\nقَالَ كَذٰلِكِ‌ ۚ قَالَ رَبُّكِ هُوَ عَلَىَّ هَيِّنٌ‌ ۚ وَلِنَجْعَلَهٗۤ اٰيَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَرَحْمَةً مِّنَّا‌ ۚ وَكَانَ اَمْرًا مَّقْضِيًّا‏(21)\n\nHe said, ‘So shall it be. Your Lord says, ‘‘It is simple for Me.’’ And so that We may make him a sign for mankind and a mercy from Us, and it is a matter [already] decided.’\nفَحَمَلَتْهُ فَانْتَبَذَتْ بِهٖ مَكَانًا قَصِيًّا‏(22)\nFA-HAMALATHO FANTABAZAT BEHI MAKAANAN QASIYYAA.\nThus she conceived him, then withdrew with him to a distant place.\nفَاَجَآءَهَا الْمَخَاضُ اِلٰى جِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ‌ۚ قَالَتْ يٰلَيْتَنِىْ مِتُّ قَبْلَ هٰذَا وَكُنْتُ نَسْيًا مَّنْسِيًّا‏(23)\nFA-AJAAA-AHAL MAKHAAZO ELAA JIZ-I’N NAKHLAH, QAALAT YAA LAYTANEE MITTO QABLA HAAZAA WA KUNTO NASYAM MANSIYYAA.\nThe birth pangs brought her to the trunk of a date palm. She said, ‘I wish I had died before this and become a forgotten thing, beyond recall.’\nفَنَادٰٮهَا مِنْ تَحْتِهَاۤ اَلَّا تَحْزَنِىْ قَدْ جَعَلَ رَبُّكِ تَحْتَكِ سَرِيًّا‏(24)\nFA-NAADAAHAA MIN TAHTEHAA ALLAA TAHZANEE QAD JA-A’LA RABBOKE TAHTAKE SARIYYAA.\nThereupon he called her from below her [saying,] ‘Do not grieve! Your Lord has made a spring to flow at your feet.\nوَهُزِّىْۤ اِلَيْكِ بِجِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ تُسٰقِطْ عَلَيْكِ رُطَبًا جَنِيًّا‏(25)\nWA HUZZEE ELAYKE BE-JIZ-I’N NAKHLATE TOSAAQIT A’LAYKE ROTABAN JANIYYAA.\nShake the trunk of the palm tree, freshly picked dates will drop upon you.\nفَكُلِىْ وَاشْرَبِىْ وَقَرِّىْ عَيْنًا‌ ۚ فَاِمَّا تَرَيِنَّ مِنَ الْبَشَرِ اَحَدًا ۙ فَقُوْلِىْۤ اِنِّىْ نَذَرْتُ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ صَوْمًا فَلَنْ اُكَلِّمَ الْيَوْمَ اِنْسِيًّا ‌ۚ‏(26)\nFA-KOLEE WASHRABEE WA QARREE A’YNAA, FA-IMMAA TARAYINNA MENAL BASHARE AHADAN, FA-QOOLEE INNEE NAZARTO LIR-RAHMAANE SAWMAA FA-LAN OKALLEMAL YAWMA INSIYYAA.\nEat, drink, and be comforted. Then if you see any human, say, ‘‘Indeed I have vowed a fast to the All-beneficent, so I will not speak to any human today.’’ ’\nفَاَتَتْ بِهٖ قَوْمَهَا تَحْمِلُهٗ‌ؕ قَالُوْا يٰمَرْيَمُ لَقَدْ جِئْتِ شَيْئًا فَرِيًّا‏(27)\nFA-ATAT BEHI QAWMAHAA TAHMELOH, QAALOO YAA MARYAMO LAQAD JEATE SHAY-AN FARIYYAA.\nThen carrying him she brought him to her people. They said, ‘O Mary, you have certainly come up with an odd thing!\nيٰۤاُخْتَ هٰرُوْنَ مَا كَانَ اَ بُوْكِ امْرَاَ سَوْءٍ وَّمَا كَانَتْ اُمُّكِ بَغِيًّا‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(28)\nYAA UKHTA HAAROONA MAA KAANA ABOOKIM RA-A SAWINW WA MAA KAANAT UMMOKE BAGHIYYAA.\nO sister of Aaron[’s lineage]! Your father was not an evil man, nor was your mother unchaste.’\nفَاَشَارَتْ اِلَيْهِ‌ ؕ قَالُوْا كَيْفَ نُكَلِّمُ مَنْ كَانَ فِى الْمَهْدِ صَبِيًّا‏(29)\nFA-ASHAARAT ELAYH, QAALOO KAYFA NOKALLEMO MAN KAANA FIL MAHDE SABIYYAA.\nThereat she pointed to him. They said, ‘How can we speak to one who is yet a baby in the cradle?’\nقَالَ اِنِّىْ عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ ؕ اٰتٰٮنِىَ الْكِتٰبَ وَجَعَلَنِىْ نَبِيًّا ۙ‏(30)\nQAALA INNEE A’BDUL LAAH, AATAANEYAL KETAABA WA JA-A’LANEE NABIYYANW.\nHe said, ‘Indeed I am a servant of Allah! He has given me the Book and made me a prophet.\nوَّجَعَلَنِىْ مُبٰرَكًا اَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُ وَاَوْصٰنِىْ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَالزَّكٰوةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا ‌ۖ ‏(31)\nWA JA-A’LANEE MOBAARAKAN AYNA MAA KUNT, WA AWSAANEE BIS-SALAATE WAZ ZAKAATE MAA DUMTO HAYYANW.\nHe has made me blessed, wherever I may be, and He has enjoined me to [maintain] the prayer and to [pay] the zakat as long as I live,\nوَّبَرًّۢابِوَالِدَتِىْ وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْنِىْ جَبَّارًا شَقِيًّا‏(32)\nWA BARRAM BE-WAALEDATEE, WA LAM YAJ-A’LNEE JABBAARAN SHAQIYYAA.\nand to be good to my mother, and He has not made me self-willed and wretched.\nوَالسَّلٰمُ عَلَىَّ يَوْمَ وُلِدْتُّ وَيَوْمَ اَمُوْتُ وَيَوْمَ اُبْعَثُ حَيًّا‏(33)\nWAS SALAAMO A’LAYYA YAWMA WOLIDTO WA YAWMA AMOOTO WA YAWMA UB-A’SO HAYYAA.\nPeace to me the day I was born, and the day I die, and the day I am raised alive.’\nذٰ لِكَ عِيْسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ‌ۚ قَوْلَ الْحَقِّ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ يَمْتَرُوْنَ‏(34)\nZAALEKA E’ESAB NO MARYAM, QAWLAL HAQQIL LAZEE FEEHE YAMTAROON.\nThat is Jesus, son of Mary, a Word of the Real concerning whom they are in doubt.\nمَا كَانَ لِلّٰهِ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ مِنْ وَّلَدٍ‌ۙ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ؕ اِذَا قَضٰٓى اَمْرًا فَاِنَّمَا يَقُوْلُ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُؕ‏(35)\nMAA KAANA LILLAAHE ANY YATTAKHEZA MINW WALADIN, SUBHAANAH, EZAA QAZAA AMRAN FA-INNAMAA YAQOOLO LAHU KUN FA-YAKOON.\nIt is not for Allah to take a son. Immaculate is He! When He decides on a matter, He just says to it, ‘Be!’ and it is.\nوَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْهُ ‌ؕ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(36)\nWA INNAL LAAHA RABBEE WA RABBOKUM FA’BODOOH, HAAZAA SERAATUM MUSTAQEEM.\n[And Jesus said,] ‘Indeed Allah is my Lord and your Lord. So worship Him. This is a straight path.’\nفَاخْتَلَفَ الْاَحْزَابُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِهِمْ‌ۚ فَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ مَّشْهَدِ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(37)\nFAKHTALAFAL AHZAABO MIM BAYNEHIM, FA-WAYLUL LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO MIM MASH-HADE YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nBut the factions differed among themselves. So woe to the faithless at the scene of a tremendous day.\nاَسْمِعْ بِهِمْ وَاَبْصِرْۙ يَوْمَ يَاْتُوْنَنَا‌ لٰكِنِ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ الْيَوْمَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(38)\n\nHow well they will hear and how well they will see on the day when they come to Us! But today the wrongdoers are in manifest error.\nوَاَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْحَسْرَةِ اِذْ قُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ‌‌ۘ وَهُمْ فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ وَّهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(39)\n\nWarn them of the Day of Regret, when the matter will be decided, while they are [yet] heedless and do not have faith.\nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نَرِثُ الْاَرْضَ وَمَنْ عَلَيْهَا وَاِلَيْنَا يُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(40)\n\nIndeed We shall inherit the earth and whoever there is on it, and to Us they shall be brought back.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ ۙ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صِدِّيْقًا نَّبِيًّا‏(41)\n\nAnd mention in the Book Abraham. Indeed, he was a truthful man and a prophet.\nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ يٰۤاَبَتِ لِمَ تَعْبُدُ مَا لَا يَسْمَعُ وَلَا يُبْصِرُ وَ لَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْكَ شَيْئًا‏(42)\n\nWhen he said to his father, ‘Father! Why do you worship that which neither hears nor sees, and is of no avail to you in any way?\nيٰۤاَبَتِ اِنِّىْ قَدْ جَآءَنِىْ مِنَ الْعِلْمِ مَا لَمْ يَاْتِكَ فَاتَّبِعْنِىْۤ اَهْدِكَ صِرَاطًا سَوِيًّا‏(43)\n\nFather! Indeed a knowledge has already come to me, which has not come to you. So follow me that I may guide you to a right path.\nيٰۤاَبَتِ لَا تَعْبُدِ الشَّيْطٰنَ‌ ؕ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ كَانَ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ عَصِيًّا‏(44)\n\nFather! Do not worship Satan. Indeed Satan is disobedient to the All-beneficent.\nيٰۤاَبَتِ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يَّمَسَّكَ عَذَابٌ مِّنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ فَتَكُوْنَ لِلشَّيْطٰنِ وَلِيًّا‏(45)\n\nFather! I am indeed afraid that a punishment from the All-beneficent will befall you, and you will become Satan’s accomplice.’\nقَالَ اَرَاغِبٌ اَنْتَ عَنْ اٰلِهَتِىْ يٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُ‌ۚ لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ لَاَرْجُمَنَّكَ‌ وَاهْجُرْنِىْ مَلِيًّا‏(46)\n\nHe said, ‘Abraham! Are you renouncing my gods? If you do not desist, I will stone you. Get away from me for a long while.’\nقَالَ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكَ‌ۚ سَاَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكَ رَبِّىْؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ بِىْ حَفِيًّا‏(47)\n\nHe said, ‘Peace be to you! I shall plead with my Lord to forgive you. Indeed, He is gracious to me.\nوَ اَعْتَزِلُكُمْ وَمَا تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَاَدْعُوْا رَبِّىْ‌ ‌ۖ  عَسٰٓى اَلَّاۤ اَكُوْنَ بِدُعَآءِ رَبِّىْ شَقِيًّا‏(48)\n\nI dissociate myself from you and whatever you invoke besides Allah. I will supplicate my Lord. Hopefully, I will not be disappointed in supplicating my Lord.’\nفَلَمَّا اعْتَزَلَهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ۙ وَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ‌ ؕ وَكُلًّا جَعَلْنَا نَبِيًّا‏(49)\n\nSo when he had left them and what they worshipped besides Allah, We gave him Isaac and Jacob, and each We made a prophet.\nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّحْمَتِنَا وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ عَلِيًّا‏(50)\n\nAnd We gave them out of Our mercy, and conferred on them a worthy and lofty repute.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ مُوْسٰٓى‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مُخْلَصًا وَّكَانَ رَسُوْلًا نَّبِيًّا‏(51)\n\nAnd mention in the Book Moses. Indeed he was exclusively dedicated [to Allah], and an apostle and prophet.\nوَنَادَيْنٰهُ مِنْ جَانِبِ الطُّوْرِ الْاَيْمَنِ وَقَرَّبْنٰهُ نَجِيًّا‏(52)\n\nWe called him from the right side of the Mount and We drew him near [to Ourselves] for confidential discourse.\nوَ وَهَبْنَا لَهٗ مِنْ رَّحْمَتِنَاۤ اَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ نَبِيًّا‏(53)\n\nAnd We gave him out of Our mercy his brother Aaron, a prophet.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِسْمٰعِيْلَ‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صَادِقَ الْوَعْدِ وَكَانَ رَسُوْلًا نَّبِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(54)\n\nAnd mention in the Book Ishmael. Indeed, he was true to his promise, and an apostle and prophet.\nوَ كَانَ يَاْمُرُ اَهْلَهٗ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَالزَّكٰوةِ وَكَانَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ مَرْضِيًّا‏(55)\n\nHe used to bid his family to [maintain] the prayer and to [pay] the zakat, and was pleasing to his Lord.\nوَاذْكُرْ فِى الْكِتٰبِ اِدْرِيْسَ‌ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صِدِّيْقًا نَّبِيًّا ۙ ‏(56)\n\nAnd mention in the Book Idrees. Indeed, he was a truthful one and a prophet,\nوَّرَفَعْنٰهُ مَكَانًا عَلِيًّا‏(57)\n\nand We raised him to an exalted station.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اَنْعَمَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ النَّبِيّٖنَ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ اٰدَمَ وَمِمَّنْ حَمَلْنَا مَعَ نُوْحٍ وَّمِنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَمِمَّنْ هَدَيْنَا وَاجْتَبَيْنَا‌ ؕ اِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُ الرَّحْمٰنِ خَرُّوْا سُجَّدًا وَّبُكِيًّا ۩‏(58)\n\nThey are the ones whom Allah has blessed from among the prophets of Adam’s progeny, and from [the progeny of] those We carried with Noah, and from among the progeny of Abraham and Israel, and from among those that We guided and chose. When the signs of the All-beneficent were recited to them, they would fall down weeping in prostration.\nفَخَلَفَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ اَضَاعُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاتَّبَعُوا الشَّهَوٰتِ‌ فَسَوْفَ يَلْقَوْنَ غَيًّا ۙ‏(59)\n\nBut they were succeeded by an evil posterity who neglected the prayer, and followed [their base] appetites. So they will soon encounter [the reward of] perversity,\nاِلَّا مَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ وَلَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ شَيْئًا ۙ‏(60)\n\nbarring those who repent, believe, and act righteously. Such will enter paradise, and they will not be wronged in the least.\nجَنّٰتِ عَدْنٍ اۨلَّتِىْ وَعَدَ الرَّحْمٰنُ عِبَادَهٗ بِالْغَيْبِ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ وَعْدُهٗ مَاْتِيًّا‏(61)\n\nGardens of Eden promised by the All-beneficent to His servants, [while they were still] unseen. Indeed His promise is bound to come to pass.\nلَّا يَسْمَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا لَغْوًا اِلَّا سَلٰمًا‌ؕ وَلَهُمْ رِزْقُهُمْ فِيْهَا بُكْرَةً وَّعَشِيًّا‏(62)\n\nTherein they will not hear vain talk, but only ‘Peace!’ Therein they will have their provision morning and evening.\nتِلْكَ الْجَنَّةُ الَّتِىْ نُوْرِثُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا مَنْ كَانَ تَقِيًّا‏(63)\n\nThis is the paradise We will give as inheritance to those of Our servants who are Godwary.\nوَمَا نَتَنَزَّلُ اِلَّا بِاَمْرِ رَبِّكَ‌ ۚ لَهٗ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْنَا وَمَا خَلْفَنَا وَمَا بَيْنَ ذٰ لِكَ‌ ۚ وَمَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ نَسِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(64)\n\n[O Gabriel, tell the Prophet,] ‘We do not descend except by the command of your Lord. To Him belongs whatever is before us and whatever is behind us and whatever is in between that, and your Lord does not forget\nرَّبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فَاعْبُدْهُ وَاصْطَبِرْ لِعِبَادَتِهٖ‌ؕ هَلْ تَعْلَمُ لَهٗ سَمِيًّا‏(65)\n\n—the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them. So worship Him and be steadfast in His worship. Do you know anyone who could be His namesake?’\nوَيَقُوْلُ الْاِنْسَانُ ءَاِذَا مَا مِتُّ لَسَوْفَ اُخْرَجُ حَيًّا‏(66)\n\nMan says, ‘What? Shall I be brought forth alive [from the grave], when I have been dead?’\nاَوَلَا يَذْكُرُ الْاِنْسَانُ اَنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَلَمْ يَكُ شَيْئًا‏(67)\n\nDoes not man remember that We created him before when he was nothing?\nفَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَحْشُرَنَّهُمْ وَالشَّيٰطِيْنَ ثُمَّ لَنُحْضِرَنَّهُمْ حَوْلَ جَهَنَّمَ جِثِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(68)\n\nBy your Lord, We will surely gather them with the devils; then We will surely bring them up around hell [scrambling] on their knees.\nثُمَّ لَنَنْزِعَنَّ مِنْ كُلِّ شِيْعَةٍ اَيُّهُمْ اَشَدُّ عَلَى الرَّحْمٰنِ عِتِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(69)\n\nThen from every group We shall draw whichever of them was more defiant towards the All-beneficent.\nثُمَّ لَنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ اَوْلٰى بِهَا صِلِيًّا‏(70)\n\nThen surely We will know best those who deserve most to enter it.\nوَاِنْ مِّنْکُمْ اِلَّا وَارِدُهَا ‌ؕ كَانَ عَلٰى رَبِّكَ حَتْمًا مَّقْضِيًّا‌ ۚ‏(71)\n\nThere is none of you but will come to it: a [matter that is a] decided certainty with your Lord.\nثُمَّ نُنَجِّى الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا وَّنَذَرُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ فِيْهَا جِثِيًّا‏(72)\n\nThen We will deliver those who are Godwary, and leave the wrongdoers in it, fallen on their knees.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا ۙ اَىُّ الْفَرِيْقَيْنِ خَيْرٌ مَّقَامًا وَّاَحْسَنُ نَدِيًّا‏(73)\n\nWhen Our manifest signs are recited to them, the faithless say to the faithful, ‘Which of the two groups is superior in station and better with respect to company?’\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ هُمْ اَحْسَنُ اَثَاثًا وَّرِءْيًا‏(74)\n\nHow many a generation We have destroyed before them, who were superior in furnishings and appearance!\nقُلْ مَنْ كَانَ فِى الضَّلٰلَةِ فَلْيَمْدُدْ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ مَدًّا ۚ‌ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا رَاَوْا مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَ اِمَّا الْعَذَابَ وَاِمَّا السَّاعَةَ ؕ فَسَيَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ هُوَ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًا وَّاَضْعَفُ جُنْدًا‏(75)\n\nSay, ‘Whoever abides in error, the All-beneficent shall prolong his respite until they sight what they have been promised: either punishment, or the Hour.’ Then they will know whose position is worse, and whose host is weaker.\nوَيَزِيْدُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اهْتَدَوْا هُدًى‌ؕ وَالْبٰقِيٰتُ الصّٰلِحٰتُ خَيْرٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ ثَوَابًا وَّخَيْرٌ مَّرَدًّا‏(76)\n\nAllah enhances in guidance those who are [rightly] guided, and lasting righteous deeds are better with your Lord in reward, and better at the return [to Allah].\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ كَفَرَ بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَقَالَ لَاُوْتَيَنَّ مَالًا وَّوَلَدًا ؕ‏(77)\n\nHave you not regarded him who defies Our signs, and says, ‘I will surely be given wealth and children’?\nاَطَّلَعَ الْغَيْبَ اَمِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمٰنِ عَهْدًا ۙ‏(78)\n\nHas he come to know the Unseen, or taken a promise from the All-beneficent?\nكَلَّا ‌ ؕ سَنَكْتُبُ مَا يَقُوْلُ وَنَمُدُّ لَهٗ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ مَدًّا ۙ‏(79)\n\nNo indeed! We will write down what he says, and We will prolong his punishment endlessly.\nوَّنَرِثُهٗ مَا يَقُوْلُ وَيَاْتِيْنَا فَرْدًا‏(80)\n\nWe shall take over from him what he talks about, and he will come to Us alone.\nوَاتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اٰلِهَةً لِّيَكُوْنُوْا لَهُمْ عِزًّا ۙ‏(81)\n\nThey have taken gods besides Allah that they may be a [source of] might to them.\nكَلَّا‌ ؕ سَيَكْفُرُوْنَ بِعِبَادَتِهِمْ وَيَكُوْنُوْنَ عَلَيْهِمْ ضِدًّا‏(82)\n\nNo Indeed! Soon they will disown their worship, and they will be their opponents.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا الشَّيٰطِيْنَ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ تَؤُزُّهُمْ اَزًّا ۙ‏(83)\n\nHave you not regarded that We unleash the devils upon the faithless to urge them vigorously?\nفَلَا تَعْجَلْ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا نَعُدُّ لَهُمْ عَدًّا‌ ۚ‏(84)\n\nSo do not make haste against them; indeed We are counting for them, a counting [down].\nيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ اِلَى الرَّحْمٰنِ وَفْدًا‌ ۙ‏(85)\n\nThe day We shall gather the Godwary toward the All-beneficent, on mounts,\nوَّنَسُوْقُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَ وِرْدًا‌ ۘ‏(86)\n\nand drive the guilty as a thirsty herd towards hell,\nلَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ الشَّفَاعَةَ اِلَّا مَنِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمٰنِ عَهْدًا‌ ۘ‏(87)\n\nno one will have the power to intercede [with Allah], except for him who has taken a covenant with the All-beneficent.\nوَقَالُوْا اتَّخَذَ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَلَدًا ؕ‏(88)\n\nThey say, ‘The All-beneficent has taken a son!’\nلَقَدْ جِئْتُمْ شَيْئًا اِدًّا ۙ‏(89)\n\nYou have certainly advanced something hideous!\nتَكَادُ السَّمٰوٰتُ يَتَفَطَّرْنَ مِنْهُ وَتَنْشَقُّ الْاَرْضُ وَتَخِرُّ الْجِبَالُ هَدًّا ۙ‏(90)\n\nThe heavens are about to be rent apart at it, the earth to split open, and the mountains to collapse into bits,\nاَنْ دَعَوْا لِلرَّحْمٰنِ وَلَدًا‌ ۚ‏(91)\n\nthat they should ascribe a son to the All-beneficent!\nوَمَا يَنْۢبَغِىْ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ وَلَدًا ؕ‏(92)\n\nIt does not behoove the All-beneficent to take a son.\nاِنْ كُلُّ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِلَّاۤ اٰتِى الرَّحْمٰنِ عَبْدًا ؕ‏(93)\n\nThere is none in the heavens and the earth but he comes to the All-beneficent as a servant.\nلَقَدْ اَحْصٰٮهُمْ وَعَدَّهُمْ عَدًّا‏(94)\n\nCertainly He has counted them [all] and numbered them precisely,\nوَكُلُّهُمْ اٰتِيْهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فَرْدًا‏(95)\n\nand each of them will come to Him alone on the Day of Resurrection.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ سَيَجْعَلُ لَهُمُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وُدًّا‏(96)\n\nIndeed those who have faith and do righteous deeds—the All-beneficent will endear them [to His creation].\nفَاِنَّمَا يَسَّرْنٰهُ بِلِسَانِكَ لِتُبَشِّرَ بِهِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ وَتُنْذِرَ بِهٖ قَوْمًا لُّدًّا‏(97)\n\nIndeed We have made it simple in your language so that you may give good news thereby to the Godwary and warn with it a disputatious lot.\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍؕ هَلْ تُحِسُّ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ اَوْ تَسْمَعُ لَهُمْ رِكْزًا‏(98)\n\nHow many a generation We have destroyed before them! Can you descry any one of them, or hear from them so much as a murmur?",
  "merits": "There are 99 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is written in the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan that the reward for reciting this Surah is equal to ten times the number of people present at the time of Prophets Zakariyyah (a.s.), Yahya (a.s.), Eesaa (a.s.), Moosa (a.s.), Ishaaq (a.s.), Haroon (a.s.), Ibrahim (a.s.), Ya’qoob (a.s.) and Ismaaeel (a.s.) combined.\nKeeping this Surah (written) in the house ensures protection from thieves and Allah (s.w.t.) blesses the occupants of the house. It is also narrated that before going in the presence of a tyrant ruler, if a person recites ‘Kaf-Ha-Ya-’Ain-Saad’ and closes, with each letter, one finger of his right hand, and then recites ‘Ha-Mim-‘Ain-Seen-Qaaf’ and with each letter, closes one finger of his left hand; and then he comes in the presence of the tyrant and recites ‘wa a’natil wojooho lil hayyil qayyoom wa khaaba man hamala zulma’ and then he opens his fingers, he will be protected from the evil of the tyrant."
}
